# Stub for the stock MTK init.mal.rc.
#
# The stock 8.1 vendor image ships this file in /vendor/etc/init/hw/ and
# init.mt6765.rc imports it unconditionally:
#
#     import ${ro.mtkrc.path}init.mal.rc
#
# The CPH1909 A.46 dump does not contain it, so without this stub init
# logs a parse error for every import attempt. MAL (MediaTek Application
# Layer) is a vendor framework component; none of its binaries or rc
# services are part of this tree, so the stub is intentionally empty.
#
# Keep the file empty (comments only): init accepts an empty rc file and
# this silences the "cannot open" error without changing boot behaviour.